{"page_id": "tables_derived-PMC5360810.1_doc-p3", "markdown": "IJCPD\n\n# Knowledge, Attitudes, and Practices of School Teachers toward Oral Health in Davangere, India\n\nTable 2: Attitudes of teachers on oral health\n\nA1. Do you think maintaining a healthy mouth is individual responsibility?\n\nTotal\n\n150\n\nPercentage 100%\n\n100\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nA2. Have you visited a dentist before?\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nTotal\n\n122\n\n28\n\nPercentage 100%\n\n81.3\n\n18.7\n\nA3. If yes, then for what reason?\n\nDecay\n\n- No\n- Sometimes\n\nPain\n\nFilling\n\nTotal\n\n471\n\n30\n\n12\n\nPercentage 100%\n\n31.3\n\n20\n\nExtraction\n\n3.3\n\nAny others specify\n\n28\n\n18.7\n\nA4. Do you think it is required to visit a dentist periodically to maintain the oral health?\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nTotal\n\n139\n\n11\n\nPercentage 100%\n\n91.3\n\n7.3\n\nTable 3: Practices of teachers on oral health\n\nP1. How do you clean your teeth?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n150\n\n100\n\n- Toothbrush and toothpaste\n- Toothbrush and toothpowder Finger and toothpowder\n\n- Yes\n- No\n\n- Neem sticks\n- Any others specify\n\nP2. How often you clean your teeth?\n\n- Mouthwash\n- Dental floss\n- Tooth picks\n- All of the above Any others specify\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n- Once daily\n- Twice daily\n- More than twice daily\n- After every meal\n\nP3. How do you brush your teeth?\n\n51\n\n99\n\n34\n\n66\n\n28\n\n- Use horizontal strokes\n- Use vertical strokes\n- Both in horizontal and vertical\n\n36\n\n65\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n18.70\n\n224\n\n43.3\n\ndirections\n\nd. Circular strokes\n\n14\n\nP4. How often do you change your brush?\n\n21\n\n90\n\n- Once in 3 months\n- Once in 6 months\n- Yearly once\n- When bristles get frayed up\n- Do not know exactly\n\n42\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n60\n\n28\n\n18\n\n12\n\nP5. What amount of paste do you apply on your brush?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\nFull length of bristles\n\n56\n\n37.3\n\nb.\n\nHalf-length of bristles\n\n86\n\n57.4\n\nPea-sized amount\n\n5.3\n\nP6. Do you press the paste in between the bristles?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n62\n\nYes\n\nb.\n\nNo\n\nP7. Do you rinse your mouth after meals?\n\n41.3\n\n58.7\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\nYes\n\nP8. Do you clean your tongue?\n\n93\n\n13\n\n44\n\n8.7\n\n29.3\n\nYes\n\nb. No\n\nP9. How do you clean your tongue?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n150 100\n\n00\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\nTongue cleaner\n\nFingers\n\n102\n\n42\n\n28\n\nToothbrush\n\nd. Any others specify\n\nP10. Do you know any other oral hygiene aids?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n143 95.3\n\n4.7\n\nP11. If you know any oral hygiene aids, then, which one do you use?\n\nTotal Percentage 100%\n\n109 72.6\n\n20\n\n13.3\n\n21\n\n14\n\n00\n\n00\n\nInternational Journal of Clinical Pediatric Dentistry, January-March 2017;10(1):89-95\n\nfor filling, 3.3% visited for extraction, and 18.7% visited dentist for other reasons.\n\nTable 3 describes practices of teachers in oral health.\n\nAll the teachers used toothbrush and toothpaste to clean their teeth. Around 34% of teachers brushed their teeth once daily and 66% do brush twice daily. Around 43.3% of teachers did brush their teeth both in the horizontal and vertical directions, 24% teachers did use vertical strokes, 18.7% use horizontal strokes, whereas 14% only used circular strokes while brushing. Majority of teachers (60%) change their toothbrush once in 3 months, 28% changed their toothbrush once in 6 months, and only 12% teachers changed their toothbrush when bristles get frayed up\n\n91", "width": 1650, "height": 2350, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "IJCPD", "bbox": {"x": 1444.362017559347, "y": 34.270833246936164, "width": 83.23442136498511, "height": 29.375000000000156}}, {"kind": "heading", "text": "Knowledge, Attitudes, and Practices of School Teachers toward Oral Health in Davangere, India", "bbox": {"x": 474.92581575923464, "y": 132.18749998311785, "width": 1057.566765578635, "height": 29.374999999999897}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Table 2: Attitudes of 